It clones the whole distribution repository and pickaxes its full git history (git log -S for the commit adding a CHECK_LOADED anchor, then installs consumer trees from BASE and THEIRS refs via scripts/install.sh), so its inputs are the entire tree plus history, which an inputs.decl file list and a one-commit seeded sandbox cannot supply.
Evidence: with inputs.decl = the gate script + fixtures/lib and git.decl=seed, hermetic-run exits rc=2 ("seed.sh: mktemp: command not found", FIXTURE ERROR: seed failed); with no git history the fixture takes its own SKIP branch and exits 0, asserting nothing.
